Z||000000||Lunapark||09-29-2000||10:56 PM||||1st question:Any one with an automatic that could answer these questions for me.<P>What is the RPM reading at 45mph, 50mph, 60mph, 70mph and 80mph.<P>2nd. I want to change the gear ratio in my 88 Auto, so at higher speeds the tach is running lower. I want to increase the top end speed and at the same time lower the rpm from the stock mode. <P>Thanks<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||09-30-2000||05:37 AM||||At 70 mph, my 88 ran at 3200 rpm.  The 88s had a final drive of 3.33 I think.  There was a thread on the forum within the last week or so that gave all the final drive ratios for the automatic transmissions.  Try a search.<BR>Great for acceleration lousy for milage.  Unless you have a close relation ship with a transmission shop or the expertise,  it gonna be big bucks to fix. I'm having a t440 put in (4 speed auto).  Even bigger bucks!<P>You may be able to increase top speed somewhat, the usual problem comes from the stock 2.8 doesn't have the hp to turn the engine any faster. Example my stock 5 speed does 2300-2400 rpm at 70 in 5th gear, now if you double the rpms to 4800, the speed should be 140.  Red line is 6500, that would be 190.  I can't push the car in 5th gear to 4500 rpm, so the only way mine would do 190 is if it were falling off a cliff.<P>By lowering the final drive rpms would improve fuel economy.  By the way, I was averaging 32-33 mph on my last weekends trip to Rutland, Ma - Kick Hill Farms and back.<P>Just filled up  300 miles 9.2 gallons.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-30-2000||08:51 PM||||Read my cave article about testing the TC lockup. That will affect engine rpm and gas millage if it's not working.<P>Assuming you have the original tranny in the car...(From a comming update to my th125 article.)<P>All TH125 transmissions are essentially the same except for the final drive gears. The following RPO codes apply to TH125c and 440 T4 transmission final drive gears.<P>FP3, FW2, FW9, F47, F90 = 3.06 <P>F16, F17, F62, F75 = 2.84<P>F77, F79, GX3 = 3.33<P><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-30-2000).]||||reg||1
